`python3 test_impl.py` now prints `ALL PASS` (stress loop took 7.1s). I ran it after each function, and `test_impl.py` is untouched.

- **`encode`** (`rle.py`): groups consecutive characters and emits each character followed by its run count.
- **`decode`** (`rle.py`): reads character-plus-digits pairs and expands them.
- **`merge`** (`intervals.py`): sorts by start and folds each interval into the previous one when it overlaps or touches. It returns new lists and does not modify the input.

One limitation of the format itself: strings containing digits don't round-trip (`encode("1111")` gives `"14"`, which decodes as four `1`s only by luck; `"a11"` is ambiguous). The docstrings don't address this and the tests don't exercise it, so I left it as is.

Nothing is committed; the run also left an untracked `__pycache__/` directory.
